A. Rates by arithmetic from JPL "Approximate Positions of the Planets", Table 2a, mean longitude rates in
   degrees per Julian century, ecliptic and equinox of J2000 (fetched 23 Nov 2026):
   planet: synodic cycles per turn of the Sun (sky | gears); error of the gears, deg per Julian year, by
   arithmetic | measured in the tables | printed in the 2021 paper; arithmetic over printed
   mercury  3.15209105 | 3.15208333   -0.002780 | -0.002788 | -0.005022   0.553
   venus    0.62552319 | 0.62554113   +0.006458 | +0.006453 | +0.008576   0.753
   mars     0.46831576 | 0.46830986   -0.002124 | -0.002120 | +0.003089   0.688
   jupiter  0.91569565 | 0.91569767   +0.000728 | +0.000645 | +0.000802   0.908
   saturn   0.96605177 | 0.96606335   +0.004168 | +0.004415 | +0.004208   0.990
   (Jupiter and Saturn swing slowly against each other, about a third and four-fifths of a degree over some
   nine centuries; the tables at two dates catch that swing, the long-run rates do not.)

